{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-161257" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-161257" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the domain of integration $R=[1,4]\\times [0,2]\\times [0,\\pi /2]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\,dx{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,dy{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\,dx{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,dy{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,dz & =(4-1)\\cdot (2-0)\\cdot [\\operatorname{sin}⁡z]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =6\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-161257" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "55bf72684dc66cd996eb875edbd56a08142515b03b434d9c97957f5d123de1f6"} {"question" "q-161257" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-161257" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "3\\pi "] ["math" "6"] ["math" "6\\pi "] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-161257" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-161269" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-161269" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the domain of integration $R=[0,4]\\times [1,2]\\times [0,1]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\,dx{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy{\\int }_{0}^{1}{z}^{3}\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\,dx{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy{\\int }_{0}^{1}{z}^{3}\\,dz & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{4}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{4}{z}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(8-0)\\cdot (\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}-0) \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{7}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-161269" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "55bf72684dc66cd996eb875edbd56a08142515b03b434d9c97957f5d123de1f6"} {"question" "q-161269" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-161269" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\frac{14}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{21}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{35}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-161269" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{14}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-161295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{e}{e}^{-z}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-161295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the domain of integration $R=[0,2]\\times [0,e]\\times [0,1]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{e}{e}^{-z}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}dx{\\int }_{0}^{e}dy{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-z}\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}dx{\\int }_{0}^{e}dy{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-z}\\,dz & =(2-0)\\cdot (e-0)\\cdot [-{e}^{-z}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot e\\cdot (-{e}^{-1}+{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =2e(1-{e}^{-1}) \\\\  & =2e-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-161295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "55bf72684dc66cd996eb875edbd56a08142515b03b434d9c97957f5d123de1f6"} {"question" "q-161295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-161295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2e-2"] ["math" "4-2e"] ["math" "e-4"] ["math" "{e}^{2}-1"] ["math" "{e}^{2}-2e"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-161295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2e-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-161345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-y}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{e}^{z+1}\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-161345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-y}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{e}^{z+1}\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-y}^{0}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{e}^{z+1}\\,dz]dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-y}^{0}2[{e}^{z+1}]_{z=0}^{z=x}\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-y}^{0}2({e}^{x+1}-e)\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-y}^{0}2({e}^{x+1}-e)\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[2{\\int }_{-y}^{0}{e}^{x+1}-e\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2[{e}^{x+1}-ex]_{x=-y}^{x=0}\\,dy \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{0+1}-e(0)-({e}^{-y+1}-e(-y))dy \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}e-{e}^{1-y}-ey\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\int }_{0}^{1}e-{e}^{1-y}-ey\\,dy & =2{[ey+{e}^{1-y}-\\frac{e}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =2(e(1-0)+{e}^{1-1}-{e}^{1-0}-\\frac{e}{2}({1}^{2}-{0}^{2})) \\\\  & =2(e+1-e-\\frac{e}{2}) \\\\  & =2-e\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-161345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "55bf72684dc66cd996eb875edbd56a08142515b03b434d9c97957f5d123de1f6"} {"question" "q-161345" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-161345" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2(e-1)"] ["math" "2-e"] ["math" "3e"] ["math" "4({e}^{2}-2)"] ["math" "{e}^{2}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-161345" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2-e"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-162536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{\\int }_{0}^{y}xyz\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-162536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{\\int }_{0}^{y}xyz\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}xyz\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{[\\frac{1}{2}xy{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{2}xy({y}^{2}-0)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{2}x{y}^{3}\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{2}x{y}^{3}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{2}x{y}^{3}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{8}x{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{8}x({x}^{4}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{5}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{5}\\,dx & =\\frac{1}{8}{[\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{6}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{48}(64-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-162536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "55bf72684dc66cd996eb875edbd56a08142515b03b434d9c97957f5d123de1f6"} {"question" "q-162536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-162536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"} {"question" "q-162536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068903/state.json" "file_sha256" "558519165d9d10ff8c3fb30ddfb80d96b539ad7a558ec5ad2ea8674f2c5c9c23"}] "usage" {"q-161345" [] "q-161257" []} "basis" 2453 "retractions" [[17592186198535 :question/problem "What is $∫_{0}^{π/2}∫_{0}^{2}∫_{1}^{4}\\cos zdxdydz$?"] [17592186198536 :question/problem "What is $∫_{0}^{1}∫_{-y}^{0}∫_{0}^{x}2e^{z + 1}dzdxdy$?"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186194112 17592186194113 17592186194114 17592186194115 17592186194116 17592186194118 17592186194119 17592186194120 1759